  "descriptions": {
    "preferred": "This large-leaved cultivar has seven ovate lobes separated more than halfway to the leaf base. The lobes taper to a sharp point and have slightly serrated margins. The leaves range in size from 9 to 12 cm long and wide. The petioles are about 4 cm long. The leaves are a dark maroon-red. The color is lighter as they first unfold but assumes the very rich tones in late spring and into summer. In late summer the leaves turn green red or bronze. Fall color is a strong crimson. Thisstrong-growing,uprighttreehasabroadlyspreading crown as it matures. The branches are sturdy, and it is a hardy cultivar. It reaches 4 m high and more in width. Some early references equate this cultivar with"
  },
